    skos:definition "Plant products of low molecular weight formed primarily from oxidative coupling of two p-propylphenol moieties. They can also be described as micromolecules with two phenylpropanoid units coupled together. They can be attached in various manners, like C5-C5', C8-C8'. Most known natural lignans are oxidized at C9 and C9´ and, based upon the way in which oxygen is incorporated into the skeleton and on the cyclization patterns, a wide range of lignans of very different structural types can be formed.";
    skos:inScheme conceptscheme:chemische_stof;
    skos:narrower chemische_stof:0001510;
    skos:narrowerTransitive chemische_stof:0000047, chemische_stof:0001510, chemische_stof:VJJPUSNTGOMMGY-MRVIYFEKSA-N;
    skos:notation "CHEMONTID:0001392";
    skos:note "Plant products of low molecular weight formed primarily from oxidative coupling of two p-propylphenol moieties. They can also be described as micromolecules with two phenylpropanoid units coupled together. They can be attached in various manners, like C5-C5', C8-C8'. Most known natural lignans are oxidized at C9 and C9´ and, based upon the way in which oxygen is incorporated into the skeleton and on the cyclization patterns, a wide range of lignans of very different structural types can be formed.";
    skos:prefLabel "Lignans, neolignans and related compounds"@en;
    skos:semanticRelation chemische_stof:0000000, chemische_stof:0000047, chemische_stof:0001510, chemische_stof:9999999, chemische_stof:VJJPUSNTGOMMGY-MRVIYFEKSA-N.
