    skos:broaderTransitive chemische_stof:0000000, chemische_stof:0000147, chemische_stof:0000261, chemische_stof:9999999;
    skos:definition "A group of macrolides with a structure containing a 16-membered lactone ring fused to a 1,7-dioxaspiroundecane ring system and to either a benzofuran (or hydrogenated derivative thereof). In some cases (e.g. Milbemycin E), the tetrahydrofuranyl ring is missing. Milbemycins can be o-glycosylated at C13 to form Avermectins. Milbemycins are produced by Streptomyces species.", "A group of macrolides with a structure containing a 16-membered lactone ring fused to a 1,7-dioxaspiroundecane ring system and to either a benzofuran (or hydrogenated derivative thereof). In some cases (e.g. Milbemycin E), the tetrahydrofuranyl ring is missing. Milbemycins can be o-glycosylated at C13 to form Avermectins. Milbemycins are produced by Streptomyces species."@en;
    skos:inScheme conceptscheme:chemische_stof;
    skos:narrower chemische_stof:SPBDXSGPUHCETR-MVGRHBATSA-N, chemische_stof:VOZIAWLUULBIPN-UHFFFAOYSA-N, chemische_stof:YZBLFMPOMVTDJY-UHFFFAOYSA-N, chemische_stof:ZLBGSRMUSVULIE-UHFFFAOYSA-N;
    skos:narrowerTransitive chemische_stof:SPBDXSGPUHCETR-MVGRHBATSA-N, chemische_stof:VOZIAWLUULBIPN-UHFFFAOYSA-N, chemische_stof:YZBLFMPOMVTDJY-UHFFFAOYSA-N, chemische_stof:ZLBGSRMUSVULIE-UHFFFAOYSA-N;
    skos:notation "CHEMONTID:0002902";
    skos:note "A group of macrolides with a structure containing a 16-membered lactone ring fused to a 1,7-dioxaspiroundecane ring system and to either a benzofuran (or hydrogenated derivative thereof). In some cases (e.g. Milbemycin E), the tetrahydrofuranyl ring is missing. Milbemycins can be o-glycosylated at C13 to form Avermectins. Milbemycins are produced by Streptomyces species.", "A group of macrolides with a structure containing a 16-membered lactone ring fused to a 1,7-dioxaspiroundecane ring system and to either a benzofuran (or hydrogenated derivative thereof). In some cases (e.g. Milbemycin E), the tetrahydrofuranyl ring is missing. Milbemycins can be o-glycosylated at C13 to form Avermectins. Milbemycins are produced by Streptomyces species."@en;
    skos:prefLabel "Milbemycins"@en;
